---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../../data/seo';

const meta = seo.schemas;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-website.pages.dev/';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: meta.title,
  description: meta.description,
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, meta.canonicalPath),
};
---

<BaseLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="container prose-card">
    <p class="section-kicker">Two contracts, separately versioned</p>
    <h2>Core candidate schemas</h2>
    <p>These JSON Schemas describe the experimental <strong>0.1.0-draft.1</strong> binding. Use them with the semantic validator: a structurally valid document can still have broken references, mismatched pins, or invalid transition selections.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/core/0.1.0-draft.1/schemas/bundle.schema.json" download>Bundle schema</a></li>
      <li><a href="/core/0.1.0-draft.1/schemas/definition.schema.json" download>Definition schema</a></li>
      <li><a href="/core/0.1.0-draft.1/schemas/record.schema.json" download>Investigation record schema</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p><a href="/core/0.1.0-draft.1/binding.md">Binding documentation</a> · <a href="/core/0.1.0-draft.1/coverage.md">Validation coverage</a> · <a href="/core/">Candidate release</a></p>

    <h2>Legacy graph schema</h2>
    <p>The earlier graph schema remains available for the graph release archive and legacy Graph Studio. It describes nodes and edges, not the new definition-and-record contract. Its release identifiers are unchanged.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/assets/data/core.schema.json" download>Legacy schema bundled with Graph Studio</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/tensor-standards-consortium/TENSOR-Framework/tree/main/releases/core/schemas">Published legacy schema archive</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Pin an explicit version and content digest. A mutable “latest” location is a discovery convenience, not a reproducible pin.</p>
    <p><a href="/graphs/">Legacy graph releases</a> · <a href="/implement/">Implement the new candidate</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
